cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this proof or checker, cite this archive and the sources listed in README.md."
title: "Near-Singleton conflict-checkable codes with local-to-global consistency"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yongxian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3864-3536"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
abstract: "For every length n at least 3, distance d from 2 to n-1, and positive epsilon, constructs conflict-checkable codes with local-to-global consistency and dimension at least n-d+1-epsilon. This resolves the existence conjecture following Applebaum and Kachlon's Theorem 1.8. Includes proof and exact checks; no efficient conflict decoder claim."
